WEBVTT

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.290
♪ We have no reason to stop ♪

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.080
♪ Even if they laugh at us and even if we cry ♪

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.750
♪ We’ll keep basking in the spotlight and continue singing ♪
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:42.620
♪ Yeah! Wow! OK! Yeah, yeah! ♪

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.660
Maina!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.250
Okay, then. Let's begin the Q&A section.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.370
Okay!

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.450
This is a question from
Mocchi Heart from Kita Ward.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:08.370
What clubs did you belong to in high school?

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.000
Well, Sorane?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.580
Huh? Me?

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.200
I was... in the tennis club.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.950
The tennis club?!

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.750
D'oh!

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.000
The tennis club is so gaudy!

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.540
Well, what can you do?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.000
We <i>otaku </i>can't insert ourselves
into the lives of idols.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.000
I mean, if I had the chance...

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.830
...I'd like to be reborn and be Maina's classmate!

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.910
So you're going to die right now
and be reborn immediately?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.410
Quit trying to sound so philosophical.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.040
By the way, Maina was in the going home club.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.000
To think someone can look so smug just because
their fave just went right home after school.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.750
Well, I mean, it's not like
she could've belonged

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.950
to some preppy club when she dances like that.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.500
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.250
I don't really watch her.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.410
How dare you both look so bored about this?

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.910
But if what you proposed
was actually possible, Eripiyo,

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:08.500
I'd like to be reborn as a powerful man
and let Reo have a major debut!

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.660
I know, right?!

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.660
Wait, why are you both
betting on your next life?

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.000
I want to make Sorane happy in this life.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.700
--What?
--Make her happy?

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.120
Yes! I'm going to work hard enough
to support both of us!

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.790
So I want Sorane to wait at home
for me and prepare delicious meals!

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.080
Welcome home, Motoi.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.750
That's my dream!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.950
Oh, I see. Motoi is actually in love with her.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:35.870
Huh?

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.870
You mean, that's not normal?
Did I do something wrong?

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.120
Can't relate.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.120
Huh?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.080
"Do You Like Me?"
Hey, look at that!

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.000
You'd never guess some
of those girls were in Girls' Festa

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.790
just by looking at that line...

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:34.330
Our numbers are random today,
so I figured we didn't need to hurry, but...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.040
To think there'd be this many...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.200
We will now begin distributing the tickets!

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.160
Yeah, this seems about right.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.040
Gah! I'm gonna puke!

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:07.790
Then again, there aren't that many
people here, so it's more like 30.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.660
I was gonna watch from the back today anyway.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.830
So, Eripiyo...

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.250
I've been meaning to ask...

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.540
What's with that getup?

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.910
Did you two read her interview
in this month's <i>Mellow</i>?

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.040
"OKAYAMA mellow"
"Special Interview"
"ChamJam's Maina Ichii"

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.370
Someone who's tall,
looks good in dapper scarves...

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:33.620
Oh, and I think it'd be a nice touch
if they had a mustache.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.040
That's what Maina said.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.620
Apparently, that's her type.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.450
That's her ideal guy, right?

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:47.910
Gender means nothing when it comes
to my love for Maina.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.040
Right.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.750
But I gotta hand it to Maina.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.540
She totally described someone
you'd never see in our crowd.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:59.540
Right?! My Maina's the most capable
idol in the universe!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.120
Now, hang on a second.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:07.500
My Reo would never give such
a specifically detailed answer like that.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.370
"OKAYAMA mellow"
"Special Interview"
"ChamJam's Reo Igarashi"

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.580
"OKAYAMA mellow"
"Special Interview"
"ChamJam's Reo Igarashi"
My ideal partner is whoever I fall in love with.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.700
If I had to be more specific?

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.580
Someone who's kind.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.330
Does that sound too normal?

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:18.290
See?

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.830
Oh, shut it!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.330
To each their own!

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:25.330
Maina's answers are always the right answers!

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.790
You really are a Maina stan
through and through, aren't you?

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.450
"ChamJam Concert Stage"
"Giraffe Plaza"
Thank you so much.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.450
--Thanks for coming to see me again.
--Hello. Is this our first time meeting?
--I'm right here!

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.160
I mean, nothing beats <i>oba </i>leaves
as a filling, right?

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.620
<i>Oba </i>leaves are a great medicinal herb.
They're so full of life!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.200
Good morning, Maina.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.830
I see you're still the cutest in the universe.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.250
Huh?

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.040
Um...

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.000
I'm trying out a new look.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.040
You know, since you said this was your type.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:14.910
Huh?!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.910
D-Did I mention Eripiyo?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.660
I read <i>Mellow</i>. This is your ideal type, right?

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.120
Huh? Oh!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.410
Oh, that thing.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.790
I totally forgot about that.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:32.370
I mean, you could've really written anything.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:38.450
I was just so happy you showed up in that column
that I could barely contain myself!

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.370
E-Eripiyo...

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.580
So I'll do my best to be your ideal guy!

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.200
You really don't need to...

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.500
Huh?!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.700
Are you telling me there's no point in trying?

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.870
You don't see me as anything more than a fan?

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:56.910
I want you to stay just
the way you are, Eripiyo.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:01.410
I-I wished for your major debut
on one of the haiku strips!

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.620
Wait, did I sound like I'm being
impatient for her reply?

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.200
Did you really...

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.370
...wish that?

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.000
Huh?! Yeah.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.410
Then why didn't she give me any haiku strips?

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:19.200
I want you to be the center
and appear in all kinds of things.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.660
I also... want you to go to the Budokan.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.540
I...

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:28.040
...just wanted a letter from you, Eripiyo.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:32.250
I'll spend every last yen on you, Maina.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:33.870
That's not it...

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.330
Thank you very much!

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.370
Oh, Eripiyo.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.040
Hey, how'd it go with Maina?

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:56.790
Huh?

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.040
That seems rather complicated...

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:05.790
She didn't completely act cold towards me,
though I mean, others may see it that way...

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:10.040
Maina... Is there nothing that I can do
to make you smile at me?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.040
Let's go!

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.950
Wait up!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.250
Eripiyo.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.250
The fact that they're human is so scary.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.620
Wait, what?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.370
I mean, they pretty much decide
if they love or hate you.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.580
Isn't that super scary?!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.540
I never even thought about that.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.200
Now I can't stop thinking about that, Eripiyo!

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.370
Well, I just realized it myself!

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:44.620
"Danger!!" "Humans"
Because I couldn't face this despair on my own!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.790
I wanted to make it up to you after
making us realize our newfound despair.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:58.540
So I tried to plan a way we could go see Cham
during their promotional activities this week.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.120
Unlike the zoo the other day,
we'd be able to line up in order.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:08.290
But they're going to be at
a shopping mall in the boonies.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.450
Even if we take the first train,

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:12.790
the earliest we can get there is an hour
before they start handing out tickets.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.620
That's totally not enough time, is it?

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:19.450
So I was thinking about staying
at a local internet café the night before.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.200
How does this idea sound to you, Kumasa?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.830
Of course, I'm in.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.330
Even out in the boonies,
I'm going to be cheering up front.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.660
That's my duty, after all!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.120
Okay, in that case...

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.120
Let us live our best internet café lives.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:38.870
"Inters"
"Comics and Internet"

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.290
"Motoi"
What time are you getting there today?
Let's line up together.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.080
Too bad for you!

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:04.540
We're actually already in the boonies
because we decided to stay here overnight!

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:14.040
The boonies? But they're supposed
to be playing in the city today.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.040
Wha--?

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:17.910
Wait...

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:20.580
Huh?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.080
"Schedule"

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.410
"Big City Okayama Shopping District Space"
"Boonies Shopping Mall"
I got the week wrong?!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.910
You can't be serious!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.290
You sounded so confident
that I didn't even think to check, Eripiyo!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:43.580
Well, you should've checked!
We're talking about your favorite's schedule here!

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.910
And you call yourself Maina's top <i>wota</i>?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.950
It's not like I wanted to be!

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.870
It's so according to the schedule...

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.370
I want to drive the train myself...

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:03.450
Should we take the streetcar?
No, running is faster than waiting!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.040
Make your legs longer, Kumasa!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.250
I cannot! I'm quite overweight!

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.580
Let's give up already.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:26.500
Even if we take our time,
we'll still make it to the special fan event.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.040
What?!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:31.870
I'm not an idol <i>wota </i>just as
a leisurely pastime because I'm rich!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.040
But if you insist, I'm just gonna run ahead.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.870
Man, I'm so happy I have long legs!

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:42.000
I knew this would happen, but it still hurts.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.500
Hello, everyone!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.250
We're ChamJam.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.700
Hello!

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:01.120
Huh? Eripiyo's not in the front row?

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.700
I wonder what happened.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.160
We're starting with our usual first song.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.790
We look forward to hearing those chants!

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.290
One, two, three, four!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.500
Eripiyo's that far back?

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.580
And she's soaked.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.040
Was she late because she fell into a river?

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:28.660
♪ I get lonely easily and need you to dote on me ♪
It's a girl. I've never seen one here before.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.040
She's soaked...

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.000
Wait, Maina.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.370
Huh?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.370
Your heart rate...

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.410
Okay, it's normal.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.580
Yes.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:43.830
Eripiyo's trying things by trial and error.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.410
I'm not sure how to respond.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.830
Thank you very much!

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:51.160
Well, see you at the studio tomorrow!

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.160
Eripiyo...

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.580
I'm wide open, people!

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:01.500
Oh, come on. I'm here.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.830
I guess you are.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:07.450
You're in my line so often
that you're basically the same as air.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.290
Man, I wish I could be like that.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:12.750
Well, Yuka is definitely the most popular
out of the back-row squad.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.290
Don't say "back-row squad."

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.330
I wish I could be like that, too.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:22.370
It definitely wouldn't suit you.
Your selling point is your current personality.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.040
You think so?

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.540
I'm wide open, people!

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:32.040
I mean, it really is wide open...

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.410
Yeah, that would be sad...

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.250
One for Maina!

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:38.250
Huh?

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.040
It's a girl!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.330
Hello!

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.620
Nice to meet you!

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:51.950
N-Nice to meet you.
Um, this was my first time seeing idols perform.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:55.370
Really? Where did you find out about us?

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:59.750
I see. So you mixed things up
with next week's schedule.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.950
I really have no idea why I didn't notice.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.330
--Big Brother.
--Hey.

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.750
Huh?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.660
Oh, this is my little sister, Rena.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.950
Hello.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.700
You have a real little sister?!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:12.950
Hello.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:16.120
I saw you in the very back earlier.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:19.040
I wasn't brave enough to move up front.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.660
Um... I'm not really sure
if I should say this, but...

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.870
...she looks just like Sorane.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.040
What?!

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.950
Is Sorane the girl you like?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:34.830
That's creepy.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.160
You're wrong! I mean, you're right, but...

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.330
It's not like I like Sorane because
she looks like my little sister!

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.200
I know.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:46.330
So who's your favorite?

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:51.830
Um... The girl I saw at Girls' Festa
when I went with my brother.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:55.620
I thought Maina looked cuter
than anyone else there.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.700
Maina?

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:04.120
For real? Someone finally realizes
how amazing Maina is, Kumasa!

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:06.410
Oh, man! I can barely contain myself!

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.620
Good for you.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:08.750
Rena!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.500
Let's line up together tomorrow
for their usual performance!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.750
Thank you very much.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:21.290
Oh, no!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.540
I went ahead and bought
all of them like I usually do!

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.910
But Rena's here, too...

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.950
--Um, Eripiyo...
--Gulp.

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:30.700
Hello there.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:34.370
I was told that they were
sold out of Maina's merch.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.200
Would you mind sharing some of yours with me?

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:40.160
I'm so sorry! Yeah, sure.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.410
How many do you want?

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.660
Huh? Just one is fine.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.660
Just one?!

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:46.910
Yes.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:50.450
Those in line for Maina,
please wait along the wall.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:53.160
What did you and Maina talk about yesterday?

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:59.540
Um... Just that I saw her at Girls' Festa
and that I'll continue to support her.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.660
Nice! So how did Maina respond?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.910
I'm so happy to have a girl fan!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.870
I hope I get to see you again! I'll be waiting!

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.000
Is what she said.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Huh...

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:12.330
Hello!

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.950
Oh, it's the girl from yesterday.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.660
Huh?

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.620
She seems really close to Eripiyo.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.290
What's going on?

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.620
Why?

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.290
We will now begin Maina's handshake sessions.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.580
Thank you.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.790
Everyone waiting, please step forward.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.080
I'm so nervous.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:32.450
You've got this, Rena!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:37.250
Maina's a bit shy, but if you initiate
the conversation, she'll totally reply.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.620
If you run out of things to talk about,
she likes being complimented about her dancing.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:42.540
Hello.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.540
Hello! You came to see me again!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.330
Did you have fun today?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.700
Y-Yes.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:52.000
Maina's chatting her up like no other!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.330
I'm glad they brought me.

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.950
Wait, Eripiyo brought her?

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:01.000
Y-You must've made a friend really quickly.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.450
That's great.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.450
Friend?

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:09.870
Oh, no. She just happens to know my brother.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:11.160
Oh, I see!

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.910
Maina's having way more fun
than I've ever witnessed before!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.660
Everyone should fall in love with Maina!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.580
I want her to belong to everyone!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:28.160
I never realized this because
I was the only Maina stan, but...

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.250
Thank you so much!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.120
But, like...

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.080
Please come see me again!

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.080
But...

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:38.160
I don't want to see Maina smiling
at anyone else other than me!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:42.120
Did I act too excited?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.660
Eripiyo totally saw that, too.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.540
"Maina"
Just one.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.540
--Just one?!
--Just one?!

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:54.330
I mean... If Rena got all that
with one ticket...

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.080
I should be able to, too.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.370
Why just one?

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.830
Actually, I still have 28 more.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:08.910
In order for her to go to the Budokan,
she has to become more popular.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.950
I can't do anything about that all on my own.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:18.040
When did I become so selfish?

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.580
There's something wrong with Eripiyo...

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.700
Eripiyo.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.910
Do you like me?

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.660
Huh? Of course, I do! I love you!

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.660
I mean... I tell you that all the time.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:35.580
No... What I really want to know is...

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:37.620
Thank you very much!

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:45.620
There was something wrong with Maina today.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.290
Eripiyo!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.160
Hey!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.410
Rena.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.830
Yes?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:59.410
As fellow Maina fans, let's continue
to talk about how cute Maina is.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:02.540
Sounds good. I look forward to it.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.660
Though I won't be able to come by that often.

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:08.330
You can't? Oh, I see!

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.870
Stop it! Stop being happy, me!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.160
Yes. I'll be trying to get into college.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.040
R-Right...

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.330
"Part-timer"

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:43.950
Huh?

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.950
Maina outside of work!

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.580
I've basically never seen her like this.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:55.290
She's wearing white in her normal clothes.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:58.000
I always just associate her with salmon pink.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:07.870
There's an angel...

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.160
There's an angel...

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.080
...right here on this train.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.870
Sorry, I'll change cars.

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:23.870
I'm getting off at the next stop anyway.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:25.790
Um... okay.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.870
Thank you for...

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:38.410
Thank you for always coming to shake my hand.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:46.910
You can say, "for cheering me on"
or, "giving me your undying support" there.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.790
It's not because she's human.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.620
It's because she's Maina.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.040
That's why I'm scared.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:02.620
I'll continue to come shake your hand even more.

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:16.830
I love you.

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:23.450
I love that...

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:26.200
...about you!

00:24:05.660 --> 00:24:09.450
"Next episode preview"
"#Fumi" "#YukaStan" "CV: Tomokazu Sugita"
Yuka, don't get too excited
at the Autumn Sports Festival and get hurt.

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:11.870
What are you into lately, Yuka?

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:13.790
Did you like the present
I gave you the other day?

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:16.000
If you want anything else,
just let me know in your blog!

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.620
I look forward to seeing you again on Halloween!

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:20.000
"I Promise to Make You Number 1"
Thank you very much.
